106
00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:55.839
because that was the one we
specifically selected through that parameter.

107
00:06:55.839 --> 00:06:59.569
So, as you can see, we ran the
model graded evals in this run,

108
00:06:59.629 --> 00:07:06.908
and we did get a failure because we
intentionally passed the known bad content great so you can see that your pre-release

109
00:07:06.968 --> 00:07:10.097
evals run when you merge
your application changes to

110
00:07:10.157 --> 00:07:13.285
the main branch in a
real-world development scenario

111
00:07:13.345 --> 00:07:16.654
this would happen after
you've made changes on your dev

112
00:07:16.714 --> 00:07:20.022
branch and run your per
commit evals we're setting up a

113
00:07:20.082 --> 00:07:23.331
system to progressively
increase our confidence in the

114
00:07:23.391 --> 00:07:26.639
application as we get
closer to releasing it to users.

